network-manager-openvpn3 (0.6.0~alpha.8-1~dhcargo1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Third audit pass — correctness & hardening fixes (+13 tests):
  * service: throughput rate now clamps to 0 across an openvpn3 counter
    reset instead of logging a hugely negative B/s value.
  * service: cleanup_session aborts tasks and clears session state under
    one lock acquisition, closing a window where a concurrent --persist
    reconnect saw a half-cleaned session and was wrongly rejected.
  * service: new_secrets checks the teardown flag before each
    ProvideInput; getpwnam_r retries with a doubled buffer on ERANGE so
    users with long passwd entries keep their AccessGrant.
  * service: an IPv6-literal VPN gateway is no longer fed to DNS as a
    malformed "host:0" lookup; it now logs a clear no-IPv4-gateway error.
  * properties: http-proxy-auth-file is opened with the same hardening as
    other credential reads (O_NONBLOCK + regular-file check + 16 KiB
    cap) — a FIFO planted beside the .ovpn can no longer hang the GUI.
  * properties: a failed inline-blob write now drops the data item with a
    diagnostic instead of importing a connection that points at a
    missing certificate file.
  * properties: class_init/get_property wrapped in ffi_guard; NULL
    connection guard in get_suggested_filename.
  * editor: password-tls connections now require client cert + key at
    Apply time (validation gate agreed with the save gating); new
    "Proxy password" row makes the http-proxy-password secret editable
    from the GUI at last.

 -- Dominik Jarmulowicz <dominik.jarmulowicz@oversee.biz>  Wed, 10 Jun 2026 09:58:00 +0200

network-manager-openvpn3 (0.6.0~alpha.7-1~dhcargo1) noble; urgency=medium

  * service: the pre-Started poller timeout warning now records the last
    openvpn3 status (major/minor) and the last device_name seen, so a
    "session never reached Started" failure shows whether the backend was
    reporting progress / had created a tun device — distinguishing a
    plugin-side issue from the openvpn3 backend simply never connecting
    (server / network / netcfg). Diagnostics only; no behaviour change.

