network-manager-openvpn3 (0.6.0~alpha.6-1~dhcargo1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Second security & correctness audit pass (11 fixes, +46 tests):
    - service (HIGH): the HMAC `auth` digest chosen in the editor was
      honoured on export but silently dropped from the live-connect
      profile; build_profile now emits it, so a server pinned to a
      specific digest no longer fails the handshake while the GUI still
      shows the configured value.
    - editor (HIGH): opening a connection whose vpn.data holds a value
      outside the editor's curated cipher / auth / compress /
      data-ciphers-fallback lists (set via nmcli or import, e.g.
      CAMELLIA-256-CBC, compress=stub) and clicking Apply silently
      deleted the directive; the combo now preserves an out-of-vocabulary
      value as an extra entry so it round-trips unchanged.
    - auth-dialog: the per-secret flags check masked NOT_SAVED (0x2)
      instead of NOT_REQUIRED (0x4), so a password flagged "ask every
      time" was never prompted and activation failed with no dialog; it
      now masks 0x4.
    - service: CONN_DONE (a terminal openvpn3 tunnel-DOWN event) was
      mapped to "connected" rather than "stopped", so NM kept showing the
      VPN up for ~30 s after a backend-initiated teardown.
    - service: full-tunnel redirect-gateway connections were mis-reported
      to NM as never-default — openvpn3 installs the def1 split
      (0.0.0.0/1 + 128.0.0.0/1), not a literal 0.0.0.0/0 — so the VPN's
      DNS lost system-wide priority; has_default_route now recognises it.
    - properties: an imported `keysize` was dropped from vpn.data;
      IPv6-literal `remote` values were corrupted by the vpn.data <-> .ovpn
      encode/decode (now bracket-aware on both sides); a no-type
      `verify-x509-name` value containing a colon was mis-split into name
      + a bogus type (guarded on the openvpn type keywords in both the
      service and editor emit paths).
    - properties: the http-proxy auth-file password read on import is now
      zeroized, matching the editor's existing scrub discipline.
    - service: a Disconnect racing NewSecrets no longer surfaces a
      spurious authentication failure for a deliberate disconnect; the
      --persist flag is now honoured (it was parsed but ignored, so the
      process always exited on Disconnect).

 -- Dominik Jarmulowicz <dominik.jarmulowicz@oversee.biz>  Tue, 02 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0200

network-manager-openvpn3 (0.6.0~alpha.5-1~dhcargo1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Security & correctness audit fixes across all five crates:
    - service (CRITICAL): a Disconnect arriving while a Connect was
      still in flight could leave a live, orphaned openvpn3 session up
      after the process exited — NM believed the VPN was torn down while
      the tunnel stayed connected. Disconnect now serialises against
      do_connect via a shared lock and a plugin-owned teardown flag
      (new ConnectCoordinator, unit-tested) so an in-flight Connect
      either bails and tears down its half-built session or completes
      and is torn down normally.
    - service: backend error chains are no longer forwarded verbatim to
      the D-Bus caller (info disclosure); a generic message is returned
      and the full chain stays in the service log.
    - properties: the .ovpn import open() now sets O_NONBLOCK so a FIFO
      planted at an attacker-controllable import path can no longer hang
      the host GUI thread (matches the service-side profile read).
    - properties: http-proxy-auth-file is now accepted only as a bare
      filename beside the .ovpn, closing an intermediate-directory
      symlink-traversal that could redirect the credential read.
    - editor: opening an existing connection and clicking Apply without
      retyping a password no longer wipes the stored secret — empty
      secret fields are preserved rather than removed, since secrets are
      not loaded into the dialog.
    - client: session endpoint property-read failures are now logged
      instead of being silently swallowed; the masked-input flag from
      openvpn3's UserInputQueue is carried through to InputSlot.
    - build: pin panic = "unwind" so the cdylibs' FFI catch_unwind
      guards can't be silently defeated by a future panic = "abort".

