network-manager-openvpn3 (0.6.0~alpha.3-1~dhcargo1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Review-driven hardening + i18n sweep:
    - service: AccessGrant the openvpn3 session to the connection's
      owning user resolved from NM's connection.permissions
      (user:NAME), falling back to the /run/user heuristic only for
      system-wide connections; public_access is deliberately left unset
      so session management isn't opened to every local UID. Documented
      the race-safe ip4-emit memory ordering and the NM-initiated
      Disconnect Failure-suppression path.
    - editor: HIG/i18n refactor — user-visible strings wrapped in tr()
      for gettext extraction.
    - i18n: new po/POTFILES.in and `make pot` target (xgettext over the
      Rust sources); regenerated nm-openvpn3.pot template.
    - editor: ignored end-to-end FFI smoke test driving the editor
      factory through GType registration + the GInterface vtable
      (run under xvfb-run).
    - ci: build/test/clippy now run --locked so an unrelocked
      dependency bump fails CI.
    - packaging: README note that debian-vendored/ is a read-only
      diffing snapshot; packaging changes belong on rust/upstream-deps.

